t recalculate because underlying node controls are non-functional\", \"actual\": \"Expected the Coverage % / Avg Level metric cards to recalculate immediately when a competency's level, weight, or enabled state is changed on the graph. Since the node-level Weight slider, Level bar buttons, and Enable/Disable switch do not register any state change on click, drag, or keyboard interaction (see FT-4, FT-5, IX-13, IX-20), the displayed Coverage % and Avg Level values never changed across all attempted edits, so real-time recalculation could not be observed or confirmed.\", \"evidence\": \"Coverage %/Avg Level metric card values remained identical before and after all node-control interaction attempts (switch click, level-button click, weight-slider drag).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Critical Path list does not update because underlying node controls are non-functional\", \"actual\": \"Expected the Critical Path competency name list in the metrics panel to update when a competency's critical/enabled status or level is changed. Since clicking the Level bar buttons and the Enable/Disable switch on graph nodes produced no DOM state change whatsoever (verified via aria-checked and button class inspection before/after), the Critical Path list content never changed and could not be confirmed to react to edits.\", \"evidence\": \"Code Review node level-button classes identical before/after click: 3x bg-level-intermediate + 2x bg-muted (target 5th/last button click had no effect).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Ran the Recruitment simulation with default preset adjustments (technical Level Change -1, domain Level Change -1, behavioral Weight Change +10%). Risk Gaps metric updated from 0 to \\\"1 identified\\\" and a Competency Gap Alert banner appeared with correct content: \\\"1 competency below recommended level: System Design. Consider increasing training focus or adjusting expectations.\\\" Values were valid (no NaN), Coverage 56%, Avg Level 2.7.\"}]}"
